      {
        "name": "ask",
        "description": "Ask a natural-language question about Redis. Returns a prose answer plus the source documents behind it — any `sources[].id` can be passed to `fetch`. If the documentation does not cover the question, the answer says so.\n\nReserve `ask` for a question spanning several areas of the documentation, where no single page answers and the parts interact — or when a `search` has come back empty or off-target. `ask` takes several seconds, so use `search` and `fetch` for anything narrower.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "question": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "question"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "outputSchema": {
          "properties": {
            "answer": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "sources": {
              "items": {
                "description": "One document behind an `ask` answer, as returned on the public surface.\n\n`id` is a fetch-verified `doc_id` (a page path like `commands/xadd` or a\nsection chunk like `page#sec:anchor`); passing it to `fetch` is guaranteed\nto resolve. `snippet` is a bounded excerpt from exactly the chunk `id`\npoints to, so a caller can confirm a claim without a second `fetch`.\n\n`snippet` is absent when the chunk holds nothing that could support a claim —\nan empty body, or unparsed front matter (see `_build_snippet`). The source is\nstill returned: `id`, `title` and `url` carry it, and the id stays fetchable.",
